  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Businessman Matteo de Nora approached rebuilding Team New Zealand as an exercise in making limited resources effective. Working with chief executive Grant Dalton, he valued the team's progress as well as race victories. His contribution included advising Dalton on difficult personnel decisions and taking a longer view while the chief executive handled immediate problems.\n\nDe Nora also funded a tinnitus research fellowship and the Neurology Research Unit at the University of Auckland. His support for the Tinnitus Research Initiative helped researchers share findings internationally. New Zealand appointed him a Companion of its Order of Merit for his contributions to sailing and neurological research.",
